  "worked_solution": "The numerator here is a bounded, oscillating function with \n\n$$\n|\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x|\\le 1.\n$$\n\nHowever, the denominator $x$ grows without bound as $x\\to \\infty .$ Since the denominator grows much faster than the (bounded) numerator, we conclude that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{x}=0.\n$$\n\nWe can see this from the graph of $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x}{x},$ shown below:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13979528/assets/e164233abcdf9062fd856a100fb7b792912fa030746a63f01ca7fd6683bf7f09.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
